ull,"additionalInfo":"Custom","affectedStops":[]},"nrIncident":{"id":"96FF0E2DC8904084AF97A44591C011A7","version":"20261119000102","summary":"Disruption to Thameslink services between Strood and Rainham (Kent) expected until the end of the service","routes":"Thameslink services between Kentish Town / Gravesend / Strood and Rainham (Kent)","message":"Urgent repairs to the railway between Strood and Rainham (Kent) mean that all lines are blocked. Thameslink trains running through these stations will be cancelled as a result.\nThis is expected to be the case until the end of service.\nCustomer advice:\nNo trains are be able to run between Strood and Rainham. You will need to use an alternative route to reach your destination.\nYou should allow at least an additional 45 minutes to complete your journey today.\nPlease talk to station staff, look at the information boards or check your journey planner for the most recent information.\nBus replacement:\nThameslink have been able to source some replacement buses, so you may be able to use these to get to your destination.\nSchedules for these buses will be shown on journey planners, so you can see the next services from your station\nCan I use my ticket with another operator?\nYou can travel on the following services at no additional cost;\n• Thameslink services between London Bridge and Rainham\n• Southeastern services between London Bridge and Rainham\nPlease be aware that using alternative travel will add at least 30 minutes to your journey depending on the route.\nPlanning your journey:\nFor help planning your journey, check live departure boards, view a live network map or see alternative route guides.\nIf you’re travelling within London, you can use the TfL Journey Planner.\nCan you tell me more about the incident?\nThameslink have been made aware of a track defect that requires urgent repairs.\nFor the safety of our customers and staff, trains will be cancelled while engineers carry out the necessary work.\nCheck before you travel:\nYou can check your journey using the National Rail real-time Journey Planner.\nFor helpful advice if you need to travel on a rail replacement service, including accessibility and bicycle information, please use our Rail Replacement Services page.\nYou can find the pick-up and drop-off location of rail replacement services by checking station signage or by searching for your station on our Find a Station page.\nPlease be advised that replacement vehicles may be busier than usual, and you should allow extra time for your journey.\nCompensation:\nYou may be entitled to compensation if you experience a delay in completing your journey today. Please keep your train ticket and make a note of your journey, as both will be required to support any claim.","start":"2026-11-18T23:00:00.000+00:00","end":null,"planned":false}}]},{"id":"tram","name":"Tram","mode":"tram","statuses":[{"severity":10,"description":"Good Service","reason":null}]},{"id":"transpennine-express","name":"TransPennine Express","mode":"national-rail","statuses":[{"severity":10,"description":"Good Service","reason":null}]},{"id":"transport-for-wales","name":"Transport for Wales","mode":"national-rail","statuses":[{"severity":10,"description":"Good Service","reason":null}]},{"id":"victoria","name":"Victoria","mode":"tube","statuses":[{"severity":10,"description":"Good Service","reason":null}]},{"id":"waterloo-city","name":"Waterloo & City","mode":"tube","statuses":[{"severity":20,"description":"Service Closed","reason":"Waterloo and City Line: Service will resume at 06:00. ","validity":[["2026-11-19T00:29:45Z","2026-11-19T04:00:02Z"],["2026-11-19T00:30:00Z","2026-11-19T04:00:02Z"]],"disruption":{"category":"RealTime","categoryDescription":"RealTime","created":null,"additionalInfo":null,"affectedStops":[]}}]},{"id":"weaver","name":"Weaver","mode":"overground","statuses":[{"severity":10,"description":"Good Service","reason":null}]},{"id":"west-midlands-trains","name":"West Midlands Trains","mode